{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous than I.</b> When they brought him the seal, the cord, and the staff, he acknowledged immediately, and said, ״She is more righteous than I״ — meaning, she is righteous in her words; she is with child by me. And so is the opinion of the Targum." "<b>And the Ramban</b>, of blessed memory, explained ״She is more righteous than I״ — more than me: for I intended fornication, whereas she intended the commandment of levirate marriage. And this is what he said, ״for therefore I did not give her to Shelah my son״ — meaning, she did rightly in doing so, since I did not give her to Shelah my son, for Shelah is the levir and I am the redeemer after him, should he not wish to take his levirate widow." "<b>And in the Midrash,</b> ״She is more righteous than I״ — a Bat Kol went forth and said, ״It is from Me, and from Me these things went forth.״ And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted in the last chapter of tractate Makkot: Rabbi Elazar said, In three places the holy spirit shone forth — in the court of Shem, in the court of Samuel, and in the court of Solomon. In the court of Shem: Judah said, ״She is righteous,״ and the holy spirit said, ״from Me.״ In the court of Samuel, as it is said (1 Samuel 12:5): ״HaShem is witness in you, and His anointed this day,״ and it says, ״And he said, Witness״ — it should have said, ״And they said,״ but the holy spirit responds, ״Witness.״ In the court of Solomon, as it is said (1 Kings 3:27): ״Give her the living child, and the dead one you shall not slay,״ and the holy spirit responds to him: ״She is his mother.״" "<b>And he did not know her again.</b> After he fulfilled the commandment, even though she was permitted to him all his days. And the intent of the saying ״and he did not know her again״ is and he did not cease — that is, she is permitted to him, and she was designated for him from Heaven."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:44.929256361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}